{{Quote|Some battles simply can't be won. By the time we got to Quell, it was clear that the Separatists had the upper hand and weren't about to loosen their grip. Our only choice was to rescue Jedi General Aayla Secura from her flagship before it plummeted to the planet below. The Republic lost three Star Destroyers and a lot more good soldiers that day. It wasn't our best effort, but at least we lived to fight again&mdash;barely.|Rex, ''The Secrets of the Clone Troopers''|<ref name="SecretsCloneTroopers">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Clone Troopers]]''</ref>}}
'''Quell''' was a terrestrial [[planet]] located in the [[Quell system]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. In [[21 BBY]], the planet served as a site of a [[Clone Wars]] [[Battle of Quell|engagement]], where the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Aayla Secura's task force|task force]] of [[Jedi General]] [[Aayla Secura]] was attacked by a [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] [[TF-1726's squadron|squadron]] of [[frigate]]s [[Commanding officer|commanded]] by the [[T-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid|T-series tactical droid]] [[TF-1726]]. During the battle, the Republic forces were inflicted with heavy casualties as the Confederacy claimed victory.

==Description==
{{Quote|We're entering the atmosphere.|Aayla Secura, during the Battle of Quell|<ref name="Jedi Crash" />}}
Quell was a largely unremarkable<ref name="HC 73">{{HelmetCollectionCite|73|Highlights of the Saga}}</ref> terrestrial<ref name="Quell card" /> [[planet]]<ref name="HC 73" /> located in the far reaches of<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> the [[Nuiri sector]]'s<ref name="Appendix" /> [[Quell system]]<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> and the distant reaches of [[the galaxy]],<ref name="Battles">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref> in the regions known as the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> and [[New Territories]].<ref name="New Territories" /> Situated in grid square Q-6 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]], Quell was located along<ref name="Map" /> the [[Salin Corridor]] [[hyperspace route]],<ref name="Salin" /> which connected it to the astronomical object [[Yalbec Prime]] and<ref name="Map" /> the planet<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Lola Sayu]].<ref name="Map" /> Viewed from [[Realspace|space]], the planet's surface was [[Color|cerulean]] in color<ref name="Episode Gallery">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/jedi-crash-episode-gallery|text="Jedi Crash" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Slide 1}}</ref> and its [[atmosphere]] featured white [[cloud]]s.<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> Quell had a brown terrain with large spherical formations sprouting out of the ground.<ref name="Quell card" />

==History==
{{Quote|Hurry, Skywalker. We're depending on you.|Aayla Secura, after her forces begin to suffer heavy casualties|<ref name="Jedi Crash" />}}
[[File:Battle_of_Quell2.png|thumb|left|300px|Aayla Secura's forces engaged a Separatist squadron in Quell's atmosphere.]]
In [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> during the [[Clone Wars]] fought between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], the Republic [[Aayla Secura's task force|task force]] of three [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-class Star Destroyers]], including the [[Liberty (Venator-class)|''Liberty'']], [[Commanding officer|commanded]] by [[Twi'lek]] [[Jedi General]] [[Aayla Secura]] came under [[Battle of Quell|attack]] by a Confederacy<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> [[Confederacy of Independent Systems Navy|naval]] [[TF-1726's squadron|squadron]]<ref name="Battles" /> of five [[Munificent-class star frigate|''Munificent''-class star frigates]] led by the [[T-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid]] [[TF-1726]].<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> As the [[Space warfare|battle]] raged, Secura's [[327th Star Corps]] [[clone trooper]]s experienced heavy casualties, while the Republic [[Star Destroyer|vessels]] descended from [[orbit]] into the planet's upper atmosphere, where the attacks further intensified.<ref name="Battles" /> Informed of Secura's situation over Quell, fellow [[Jedi]] [[General]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and his [[Padawan]], [[Ahsoka Tano]], reached the planet's orbit aboard the ''Venator''-class Star Destroyer ''[[Resolute]]''.<ref name="Jedi Crash" />

Arriving over Quell, as the Twi'lek Jedi lost her accompanying pair of [[Starship|Star Destroyers]], Skywalker launched several [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]] [[gunship]]s from his [[flagship]] in order to board the ''Liberty'' and rescue Secura. A Republic [[Unidentified Consular-class cruiser (Quell)|''Consular''-class cruiser]] proceeded to dock with the ''Liberty''{{'s}} lower [[hangar]] as per Skywalker's orders in an effort to extract the Jedi and return to the ''Resolute''. However, as the Jedi and several [[Cloning|clone]] [[trooper]]s, including [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]], [[Lucky]], [[Flash]], and [[Cameron]], boarded the [[Consular-class cruiser (Charger c70 retrofit)|frigate]], Skywalker was injured while attempting to hold back an explosion using [[the Force]] in order to allow his compatriots to enter the [[Frigate|ship]]. While fleeing from the ''Liberty''&mdash;which plummeted to Quell's surface&mdash;and returning to the ''Resolute'', the frigate suffered damage from crossfire and was forced to activate its [[hyperdrive]]. The vessel thus entered [[hyperspace]], departing to the planet [[Maridun]], while the Republic's remaining forces continued to engage the Confederacy in Quell's atmosphere.<ref name="Jedi Crash" />

[[File:Secura-327-art-canon-cropping.png|thumb|right|300px|Aayla Secura and the 327th returned to Quell later in the Clone Wars.]]
After the battle had ended at Quell, the Confederacy had secured an unqualified victory over the Republic, which revealed the latter's struggles in maintaining control throughout the Outer Rim Territories, where acts of separatism had begun to flourish. In addition, the Battle of Quell also underscored how ultimate Republic victory in the war over the Confederacy was not truly certain.<ref name="Battles" />

Later in the war, by the time [[Phase II clone trooper armor]] had been introduced, Secura and her troops returned to Quell and engaged in a battle on its surface.<ref name="Quell card" /> In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="DateNeyo">"[[Neyo's Almanac of Clankers]]" establishes that it was written after the [[mission to Mokivj]], but while the [[Clone Wars]] was ongoing, which places it in [[19 BBY]] per ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''.</ref> Quell was mentioned in an intelligence report by [[Clone Commander]] [[Bly]] describing [[B2-RP battle droid]]s, which was included in the survival compendium "[[Neyo's Almanac of Clankers]]."<ref name="Official Magazine 118">{{GermanFanCite|118|Database}}</ref> Rex later mentioned his time serving on Quell in his [[book]]&mdash;''[[The Secrets of the Clone Troopers]]''&mdash;which was published at some point following<ref name="SecretsCloneTroopers" /> the [[5 ABY]]<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> [[Galactic Concordance|end]] of the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the Republic's [[Proclamation of the New Order|successor]] state, the [[Galactic Empire]], and the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. He recalled that the battle had been one with no easy way to win, reminiscing on Secura's rescue and the loss of three Republic Star Destroyers.<ref name="SecretsCloneTroopers" />

==Behind the scenes==
Quell first appeared in "[[Jedi Crash]],"<ref name="Jedi Crash" /> the thirteenth episode of the animated series [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars''{{'}}]] [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]], which originally aired on [[January 16]], [[2009]].<ref name="Jedi Crash Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode013.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Jedi Crash}}</ref> The episode's script described the Battle of Quell as being fought in space, but it was moved to the planet's upper atmosphere for dramatic effect as the show entered pre-production.<ref name="Trivia Gallery">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/jedi-crash-trivia-gallery|text="Jedi Crash" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 2}}</ref> The planet was first identified in the [[The Clone Wars Episode Guides|Episode Guide]] for "Jedi Crash" on [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="Jedi Crash Ep Guide" /> The surface of Quell was pictured by the "Quell" card included in the [[Way of the Force]] wave of the ''[[Star Wars: Destiny]]'' card game by [[Fantasy Flight Games]]. The art used<ref name="Quell card" /> was illustrated by artist [[Chris Scalf]] and previously used in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity to depict the [[Planet/Legends|planet]] [[Saleucami/Legends|Saleucami]] in the [[2012]] reference book ''[[The Essential Guide to Warfare]]''.<ref name="TEGtW">''[[The Essential Guide to Warfare]]''</ref>

